<title>USA: Pep Boys stake cut by Mercury Asset.</title>
<headline>Pep Boys stake cut by Mercury Asset.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercury Asset Management Plc on Tuesday said it cut its stake in Pep Boys -- Manny, Moe &amp; Jack to 3,152,641 common shares, or 4.98 percent, from 5.04 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the London-based investment firm said its latest transactions include the net sale of shares in the Philadelphia-based auto parts retailer between June 20 and August 1 at prices ranging from $32.9986 to $35.462 each.</p>
<p>Mercury said it was holding shares in Pep Boys for investment purposes.</p>
</text>
